      en: "The Ndola Butterfly Habitat in Zambia's Copperbelt Province opened in 2010 on 2 hectares. It hosts over 50 butterfly species, including the African swallowtail and emperor butterfly. Features include a controlled butterfly garden with native nectar plants and a breeding lab. Visitors observe the complete metamorphosis cycle. The facility focuses on environmental education, partnering with local schools. It attracts about 10,000 visitors annually, supporting conservation awareness and eco-tourism.",
